{"candidateAnswer":"Right to Play, because they partner with Adidas and Powerade and focus on empowering children through sport in communities facing adversity.","evidence":"[D3:13 | 4:21 pm on 16 July, 2023] John: I just signed up Nike for a basketball shoe and gear deal. I'm also in talks with Gatorade about a potential sponsorship. It's pretty cool to be working with such big brands!\n[D3:15 | 4:21 pm on 16 July, 2023] John: Thanks! The Nike and Gatorade deals have me stoked! I've always liked Under Armour, working with them would be really cool.\n[D6:15 | 1:08 pm on 11 August, 2023] John: Yeah! Winning a championship is my number one goal. But I also want to make a difference away from the court, like through charity or inspiring people. Basketball has been great to me, so I want to give something back.","itemId":"urn:uuid:95afaf05-dd9f-5081-adb3-d7423bc71b6e","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:f693040c408b893627f10912a0dd197218221368b445afac58fa21fbc1c825b4","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What is a prominent charity organization that John might want to work with and why?","referenceAnswer":"Good Sports, because they work with Nike, Gatorade, and Under Armour and they aim toprovide youth sports opportunities for kids ages 3-18 in high-need communities.","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"f693040c408b893627f10912a0dd197218221368b445afac58fa21fbc1c825b4"}}]}